By Cassandra Santiago ,
10 hours ago Basketball wasn’t the only thing turning heads at the Los Angeles Lakers’ opening night on Wednesday (Oct. 21). Chloe Bailey wowed the audience, in person and online, after performing her rendition of the National Anthem. Now, fans can’t stop chattin’ about her mic being ON and the vocals on point, while a few others dropped their takes on her show ‘fit!
RELATED: Chloe Bailey Pops OFF On Social Media Users Criticizing Her Vacation Video & “No Makeup” Look Chloe Bailey Stuns Fans With Vocals At Lakers Game Chloe Bailey stepped to the mic inside Crypto.com Arena in Los Angeles and didn’t back down until the last note had the audience going off with applause! Sis wore a two-piece hot pink pantsuit, complete with rose ruffles on the bottoms and a cropped top. She paired her performance look with tall, dark grey booties and blonde-brown braids.
Clips immediately started hitting the ‘net following her National Anthem rendition, but the singer herself shared recap footage and photos on her Instagram on Thursday. She captioned the post, “Kicked off @lakers opening night with a bang! 💥 thank you for having me sing the first national anthem of the season 🏀🎤”
Fans React To Chloe’s National Anthem Performance In Chloe Bailey’s IG comment section, the loved poured in from all kinds of fans, from her music lovers to her fellow peers and even her equally talented sister, Halle Bailey, who wrote: “The voice & the shoe!” Meanwhile, Tiwa Savage commented three red heart emojis. Oh, and Chloe’s outfit, especially her heels got its flowers, too!
@aprilleudora commented, “MOST UNDERRATED 🔥🔥🔥🔥 Brains. Beauty. Aura. Fashion. TALENT. ✨”
@herseylumps wrote, “This woman never misses when it come to the vocals, choreography… nothing! 😍😍😍❤️❤️❤️❤️🙌🏾🙌🏾🙌🏾🙌🏾”
@guillermoraw_ said, “That voice >>>>”
@cyobrown added, “That woman is putting in work! Chloe, you’re an entertainer from the inner parts of your soul, through to your fingertips. We appreciate ya. We do!”
@annitafreeman_ commented, “❤️❤️❤️❤️❤️omg these heels is just NASTY IN THE BEST WAY! But the voice is beautiful 🙌🏾🙌🏾”
@danalittle21 argued, “This is literally the next best version after Whitney I said what I said💪🏿💪🏿🔥🔥🔥🔥Ya Chloe”
@raquelthecultivator added, “Can SANG down 🔥🔥.”
@sundayineden said, “The vocals NEVER decline honey! What an instrument!”
